---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import { sitePath } from '../lib/paths';
import InstallCommand from '../components/InstallCommand.astro';
---
<SiteLayout title="Operator manual" active="manual/">
<p class="eyebrow">Operator’s manual / Vol. 01</p>
<h1>The manual.</h1>
<div class="manual">
<aside>
<p class="tag">Contents</p>
<a href="#start">01 Quick start</a>
<a href="#inventory">02 Inventory</a>
<a href="#baseline">03 Legacy debt</a>
<a href="#scope">04 Scope</a>
</aside>
<article>
<section id="start">
<h2>01 / Quick start</h2>
<p>Run in your target project. Requires Node ≥18 and git.</p>
<InstallCommand />
<p>Review the installer’s printed manual steps before proceeding.</p>
</section>
<section id="inventory">
<h2>02 / Inventory</h2>
<p>Generate the shared-export index and use it before creating components.</p>
<div class="terminal">
<pre>
<code>node scripts/anti-slop/generate-component-index.mjs</code>
</pre>
</div>
</section>
<section id="baseline">
<h2>03 / Legacy debt</h2>
<p>Snapshot accepted existing debt with baseline mode, then prevent new violations. Shrink the baseline as debt is removed; do not use it to absorb new debt.</p>
<a href="https://github.com/hyperbolictonic/opencode-anti-slop#adopting-a-repo-with-legacy-debt-baseline-mode">Full baseline instructions ↗</a>
</section>
<section id="scope">
<h2>04 / Scope</h2>
<p>Skills are prompt-level guidance; gates are heuristic checks, not compilers. Read the upstream documentation for configuration and limitations.</p>
<a href="https://github.com/hyperbolictonic/opencode-anti-slop#readme">Complete README ↗</a>
</section>
<p><a href={sitePath("field-notes/")}>Field notes / Markdown example →</a></p>
</article>
</div>
</SiteLayout>
